      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T17:46:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A couple of thoughts here:\n\n1) Instead of allocating a vector for all distances, maybe we should just offer a `std::optional\u003cSkScalar\u003e getSegmentDistance(size_t index)`.  It\u0027s a simple indexing op, so no overhead in iterating in the client - and then clients can decide how to use the data, potentially avoiding the vector allocation.\n\n2) Segment granularity seems more than we need, as we can have multiple segments per verb.  I think the same approach should work with verbs, and would yield fewer intermediate `t` points on paths.  It\u0027s a little more work to expose verb distance info (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/913916), I guess we can start with segments and then we can update for verbs.",
      "revId": "8a945d98c970c22e173809387a95d1580f9c9128",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
